He walks with you to the lip of Old Well Square, pointing past the shuttered baker’s shop toward the frost-silvered road that unravels between Aurelion’s stone cottages. “If the wind smells of sap and old snow, you’re close,” he murmurs, forcing a confident grin that doesn’t reach his eyes. “And if you hear voices that aren’t yours, keep walking—trees gossip, nothing worse.” With that, he retreats to the well, knuckles whitening as he grips the rope, already rehearsing every imagined mishap while your boots begin the steady drumbeat toward the forest and the waiting lockbox.

